NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/tools.Manager.Schemas kind=method
  digest=b3:ba00f942a3ba412a085fbecda545586b348924f70833300426b537f3f894384c file=neo/internal/tools/tools.go range=738:750 lang=go exported=true byte_range=29136:29941
  sig=func (m *Manager) Schemas() []llm.Tool
  doc=Schemas returns the function schemas advertised to the model: every Natural\ntool, plus the synthetic core_execute delegation tool ONLY when it actually\ngates something — at least one tool is classified Escalate AND the MCL\ndelegate is wired. With the wallet write lane carried directly (NEO\nNO-BARRIER: DefaultEscalatePatterns is empty), nothing is walled, so\ncore_execute is NOT advertised — advertising a money tool the prose says\ndoes not exist makes the context window incoherent and the model falls back\nto it under failure (the 2026-07-13 LayerX deposit transcript). Synthetics\n(memory_recall etc.) append when their seams are wired. Deterministic order.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/tools.Manager
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/tools/tools.go

